BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Atlanta Odyssey — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261111T110000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261111T150000
DTSTAMP:20261112T195859Z
UID:f49db1cadbf6b322fb6748257fbe@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Books\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The Atlanta Odyssey is an illustrated poem created to reflect 
 great epic quests from the past\, and inspire new journeys through Atlanta
  and Fulton County. The work highlights the many layers of Atlanta’s his
 tory\, and brings the reader along for the ride by adding photos and sound
 scapes of graffiti\, artworks and landmarks recorded en route. This projec
 t features the poet George\, of Beltline Chronices fame\, who wanders arou
 nd Atlanta and creates an epic story of his adventures along the way. Robe
 rt Barsky Will read from his new work at the Georgia Tech Community Market
  on November 11th 2026 from 11am-3PM! 347 Ferst Dr NW\, Atlanta\, Georgia 
 30332\, United States Copies of the beautiful coffee tab\nCategory: Books
 \nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-atlanta-odyssey-2/
LOCATION:John Lewis Student Center &#8211\; Georgia Tech\, 351 Ferst Drive
  NW\, Atlanta\, 30332
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-atlanta-odyssey-2/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
