DESCRIPTION:Along the River Road Peter O’Neill and Lindsay French In Nor
 thwest Cambodia\, on the outskirts of Battambang’s provincial capital\, 
 on a stretch of road leading out of town along the Sankae River\, Cambodia
 ns work to rebuild their country and improve their lives 50 years after th
 e Khmer Rouge revolution. Neither urban nor rural\, neither typical nor un
 ique\, the river road is home to an historically mixed population: Khmer\,
  Chinese\, Chvea\, ethnic Vietnamese\; Buddhist\, Muslim\, Catholic\, and 
 evangelical Christian. Shops\, markets\, and small businesses line the riv
 er road. Mosques are located side by side Buddhist temples\, and a large C
 atholic compound dating to 1790 constitute important social and c\nCategor
