BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Illiberal Age? The Politics of Entrenchment — Washington\, D
 C
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261112T100000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261112T110000
DTSTAMP:20261112T195859Z
UID:1430335cc4258151a1c107187c68@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The year 2026 has been a contrasting year for the global traje
 ctory of illiberalism. While some countries are moving away from illiberal
  governments\, others are entering their own illiberal transformations. Ye
 t beyond electoral victories and defeats\, illiberalism is becoming a dura
 ble feature of our political and cultural lives\, increasingly entrenched 
 in institutions\, intellectual debates\, cultural production\, and collect
 ive imaginaries. Join Marlene Laruelle\, editor of the Illiberalism Studie
 s Program Yearbook\, and contributors Laura K. Field (Niskanen Center and 
 ILLSP)\, Zsolt Enyedi (Central European University)\, and Jean-François D
 rolet (Queen Mary University of London) for a discussion \nCategory: Acade
 mic\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/the-illiberal-age-th
 e-politics-of-entrenchment
LOCATION:George Washington University\, Washington\, DC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/the-illiberal-age-the-politics-of-entre
 nchment
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
