CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures\, Seminars and Workshops\,Providence\,
 United States
DESCRIPTION:This interactive session guides participants through the full 
 lifecycle of an oral history interview. Topics include preparing interview
  questions\, establishing consent and release forms\, ethical responsibili
 ties\, and strategies for active listening. Grounded in the Six R’s of O
 ral History Interviewing\, participants will practice interviewing through
  mock sessions\, gaining practical experience in conducting respectful\, e
 ffective oral history interviews. No prior experience with archives\, oral
  history\, or historical research is necessary. All three sessions must be
  attended to receive an Oral History Certificate.\nCategory: Lectures\, Se
 minars and Workshops\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/library/e
