UID:561b275fa4e3597db0fbcee63c9d@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Dance\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:In a season filled with busyness\, discover a Christmas tradit
 ion that brings families closer\, renews hope\, and celebrates Christ thro
 ugh the beauty of the performing arts. WELCOME TO THE GOSPEL NUTCRACKER. A
 s a unique biennial holiday experience\, emphasizing the true meaning of C
 hristmas\, talent from across Metro Atlanta and beyond will grace the stag
 e for the first of its kind\, a Gospel Nutcracker. Designed to facilitate 
 arts education for performing artists within the Metro Atlanta community a
 nd beyond\, this production curates a powerful intergenerational arts comm
 unity for performing artists of all ages and artistic levels. Gather your 
 family. Invite your friends. Create memories that las\nCategory: Dance\nOr
 iginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-gospel-nutcracker-2/
LOCATION:Ray Charles Performing Arts Center\, Morehouse College\, 900 West
  End Ave SW\, Atlanta\, 30310
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-gospel-nutcracker-2/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:National Symphony Orchestra: The Nutcracker & Cinderella — Washi
 ngton\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261122T190000
DTSTAMP:20261112T195859Z
UID:df66f96954776d54f9ff3d9605b4@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Be moved by two treasured fairy tales through the music of Tch
 aikovsky and Prokofiev\, conducted by Marie Jacquot in her NSO debut. Tcha
 ikovskys The Nutcracker Suite brings Clara\, the Sugar Plum Fairy\, and an
  enchanted Christmas Eve party to the concert stage\, while Prokofievs Cin
 derella Suite reimagines the timeless story with music that is playful and
  packed with clever turns. Between the ballets\, Jorge Federico Osorio cas
 ts a different kind of spell in Mozarts Piano Concerto No. 21\, famous for
  its slow\, haunting second movement. Three beloved works\, three worlds o
 f magic! There is a ticket limit of 8 tickets per person and per credit ca
 rd on this event.\nCategory: Arts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://cal
 endar.gwu.edu/event/national-symphony-orchestra-the-nutcracker-cinderella-
 5012
LOCATION:Lisner Auditorium\, 730 21st Street NW\, Washington DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/national-symphony-orchestra-the-nutcrac
 ker-cinderella-5012
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
