 ity\, Dr. Alvia Wardlaw\, for a conversation exploring the rich lineage of
  Black mural traditions\, with a focus on artists John Biggers and Hale Wo
 odruff. This program centers the monumental murals featured in the At The 
 Vanguard: Making and Saving History at HBCUs exhibition that highlights th
 e importance of HBCUs in commissioning\, collecting\, and preserving Black
  art. Together\, they’ll explore how these legendary artists drew inspir
 ation from the African diaspora and 20th century Mexican \nCategory: Art +
  Design\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/infinite-pasts-an
 d-ancestral-futures-the-murals-of-hale-woodruff-and-john-biggers/
LOCATION:Clark Atlanta University Art Museum &#8211\; Trevor Arnett Hall\,
  223 James P Brawley Drive SW\, Atlanta\, 30314
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/infinite-pasts-and-ancestral-futures-the
 -murals-of-hale-woodruff-and-john-biggers/
